%% render: auto
%% title: Polygon mesh versus Gaussian splat
%% desc: Two different representations. A Gaussian PLY is not a polygon mesh. Conversion is optional, lossy and must be verified.
flowchart TD
    A["Visual reference • authorized images or video"]:::slate
    B["Object geometry reconstruction • SAM 3D, SF3D, TRELLIS.2, modelling"]:::amber
    C["Multi-view scene capture • many overlapping photos"]:::teal
    D["Polygon mesh • vertices, faces, normals"]:::amber
    H["Camera calibration • COLMAP structure from motion"]:::teal
    E["Topology and UVs • retopology, unwrap"]:::amber
    I["Gaussian Splatting optimization • GPU training"]:::teal
    F["Materials and optional rig • PBR maps, skeleton"]:::amber
    J["Gaussian scene • PLY of Gaussian parameters"]:::teal
    G["Mesh viewer or renderer • Three.js, Blender"]:::green
    K["Compatible splat viewer • not a mesh renderer"]:::green
    L["Optional verified mesh conversion • lossy; result re-enters as a mesh"]:::rose
    A --> B
    A --> C
    B -->|OBJ, GLB| D
    C -->|images| H
    D --> E
    H -->|poses + points| I
    E --> F
    I --> J
    F -->|GLB, FBX| G
    J -->|splat PLY| K
    J -.->|unverified| L
